#----------------------------
# Command: [help common_attribute]
#----------------------------
[Command : lap_time]: Execution time - 000ms 000us 000ns(000000000ns)


Usage: common_attribute(common, common_attr, com_attr, attr) [expire=<second | "unset">] [pass=<passphrase | "unset">]

Discription:
    Set or Print common values for the data expiration period("expire") and passphrase("pass") used when storing
    or retrieving data in K2Hash.

    By setting these values, you can omit the expiration period and passphrase parameters in the "set(s)", "get(g)",
    "remove(rm)", "read_summary(r)", and "search(find)" commands, allowing them to use these common values instead.
    If these values are "unset" and the parameters are omitted in each command, reading and writing will be performed
    with no expiration period and no passphrase.

    Executing this command without arguments displays the currently configured expiration time(in seconds) and passphrase.

    Specifying the "expire=value" argument sets or unsets the expiration time(in seconds).
    For "value", specify the time in seconds as a decimal number. If "0" or "unset" is specified, the expiration
    time will be disabled.

    Specifying the "pass=value" argument sets or unsets the passphrase.
    For "value", specify a passphrase string. If empty or "unset" is specified, the passphrase will be disabled.

