#----------------------------
# Command: [help set]
#----------------------------
[Command : lap_time]: Execution time - 000ms 000us 000ns(000000000ns)


Usage: set(s, push, put) [expire=<second | "unset">] [pass=<passphrase | "unset">] [emfile=<embedding file>] [valuefile=<content file> | value=<contents>]

Discription:
    Set embedding data to K2Hash.

    "valuefile=<content file>" or "<contents>" is the value for embedding data to be registered in K2hash.
    Specify either "valuefile=<content file>" or "value=<contents>".
    If the "value=<contents>" value contains spaces, enclose it in double quotes(").
    If both are omitted, an empty string("") will be set.

    The "emfile=<embedding file>" is optional. If "emfile=<embedding file>" is not specified, If there is
    Preloaded embedding data, use it instead of "<embedding file>".
    You can load Preloaded embedding data using "load_embedding(em)" or "create_embedding(cem)".

    Executing this command without specifying the "expire" and "pass" arguments sets data using the
    values specified by the Common Attribute command("common_attribute").
    If the Common Attribute command("common_attribute") is also not configured, embedded data is stored
    in k2hash without setting an expiration period or passphrase.

    Specifying the "expire=value" argument sets or unsets the expiration time(in seconds).
    For "value", specify the time in seconds as a decimal number. If "0" or "unset" is specified, the expiration
    time will be disabled.

    Specifying the "pass=value" argument sets or unsets the passphrase.
    For "value", specify a passphrase string. If empty or "unset" is specified, the passphrase will be disabled.

