#----------------------------
# Command: [help get]
#----------------------------
[Command : lap_time]: Execution time - 000ms 000us 000ns(000000000ns)


Usage: get(g, print, p) [key=<k2hash key> | key="em" | emfile=<embedding file>] [noattrcheck] [pass=<passphrase | "unset">] [output=<output file>]

Discription:
    This command writes the value in the k2hash database corresponding to the embedded data to the
    specified output file.

    There are three ways to specify the key for retrieving K2Hash data:
      key=<key name>    Directly specify the K2Hash key name.
      key="em"          Use Preloaded embedding data.
      emfile=<file>     Specify the embedding data file.

    If "key" and "emfile" are omitted, Preloaded embedding data(equivalent to "key=em") is used.

    The data read from K2Hash is written to the "output=<output file>".
    If "output=<output file>" is omitted, a summary of the K2Hash data will be displayed the data length
    and FNV-1a hash value instead.

    Executing this command without specifying the "pass" argument reads data using the value
    specified by the Common Attribute command("common_attribute").
    If the Common Attribute command("common_attribute") is also unset, data will be read from
    k2hash without a passphrase.

    When "noattrcheck" is specified, reading is performed ignoring the attributes set on the K2Hash
    data. Normally, reading is affected by the set attributes(such as expire piriod time setting).

