#----------------------------
# Command: [help search]
#----------------------------
[Command : lap_time]: Execution time - 000ms 000us 000ns(000000000ns)


Usage: search(find, f) [score=<float string>] [key="em" | emfile=<embedding file>] [output=<output file>] [noattrcheck] [pass=<passphrase | "unset">]

    This command executes a vector search in K2Hash to find the embedding data closest to the value
    specified in the argument.

    Set the minimum cosine approximation value for "score=<float string>".
    This value should be set between "0.0f" and "1.0f".
    If omitted, it defaults to "0.0f," and detectes the closest value.

    To specify the embedding data using a file, use "emfile=<embedding file>".
    Alternatively, to specify Preloaded embedding data, use key="em". If both are omitted, the
    Preloaded embedding data will be used by default.

    If "output=<output file>" is specified, the detected embedding data will be written to that file.
    If omitted, a summary of the detected embedding data will be displayed.

    Executing this command without specifying the "pass" argument reads data using the value
    specified by the Common Attribute command("common_attribute").
    If the Common Attribute command("common_attribute") is also unset, data will be read from
    k2hash without a passphrase.

    When "noattrcheck" is specified, reading is performed ignoring the attributes set on the K2Hash
    data. Normally, reading is affected by the set attributes(such as expire piriod time setting).

