#----------------------------
# Command: [help create_projection_matrix]
#----------------------------
[Command : lap_time]: Execution time - 000ms 000us 000ns(000000000ns)


Usage: create_projection_matrix(create_pm, cpm) [dimension=<dimension | "default">]
                                                [bitsize=<bit count | "default">]
                                                [name=<name | "default">]
                                                [version=<version | "default">]
                                                [output=<output file>]

Discription:
    Create new Projection Matrix data and either load it as the internal Projection Matrix in the
    k2hvec library or save it to "<output file>" without loading it.

    If the generated Projection Matrix will be loaded as the internal data, do not specify "<output file>",
    "name", and "version".
    If it is specified "<output file>", the generated  Projection Matrix will be output to "<output file>"
    without loading as the internal data.

    Each argument follows the specifications below:
      <dimension>    Specify the dimension of Projection Matrix as a decimal number. If omit it or specify
                     "deffault"(def), use the default value(4096).
                     (The alias for this option is "dim" and "d".)
      <bitsize>      When creating a Binary hash, the bit size corresponds to the bit size of the Projection
                     Matrix, specify this bit size as a decimal number. If omit it or specify "deffault"(def),
                     use the default value(48).
                     (The alias for this option is "bit_size", "bit_count", "bitcount", "bit_cnt", "bitcnt",
                     "bit", and "b".)
      <name>         When saving generated Projection Matrix to "<output file>", specify the name to assign
