#----------------------------
# Command: [help calculate_binary_hash]
#----------------------------
[Command : lap_time]: Execution time - 000ms 000us 000ns(000000000ns)


Usage: calculate_binary_hash(calculate_bh, cal_bh, cbh) [key="em" | emfile=<embedding file>] [pmfile=<projection matrix file>]

Discription:
    Calculate the Binary hash value of the embedding data using a Projection Matrix.

    Please specify the embedding data using either "emfile=<embedding file>" or "key=em".
    If "key=em" is specified, the Preloaded embedding data will be used.
    If both are omitted, the Preloaded embedding data will also be used.

    Normally, the Projection Matrix used is either the "builtin" data in the k2hvec library
    or replaced it by "load_projection_matrix(pm)" or "create_projection_matrix(cpm)" commands.
    If "pmfile=<projection matrix file>" is specified, it is loaded into the k2hvec library in the
    same way as the "load_projection_matrix(pm)" or "create_projection_matrix(cpm)" command and
    it is used as Projection Matrix.
    Note that when this parameter is specified, the Projection Matrix will remain replaced for
    subsequent operations.

