#----------------------------
# Command: [help calculate_cos]
#----------------------------
[Command : lap_time]: Execution time - 000ms 000us 000ns(000000000ns)


Usage: calculate_cos(calculate_cosin_similarity, cal_cos, cos) <k2hash key> [noattrcheck] [pass=<passphrase | "unset">] [key="em" | emfile=<embedding file>] [simple]

Discription:
    Calculates Cosine Similarity value between two sets of embedding data.

    The Cosine Similarity value is calculated using the embedding data stored in K2hash and the embedding
    data specified via options(either specified embedding data file or Preloaded embedding data).

    One set of embedding data is retrieved from the K2Hash specified by the argument("<k2hash key>").
    Executing this command without specifying the "pass" argument reads data using the value
    specified by the Common Attribute command("common_attribute").
    If the Common Attribute command("common_attribute") is also unset, data will be read from
    k2hash without a passphrase.
    When "noattrcheck" is specified, reading is performed ignoring the attributes set on the K2Hash
    data. Normally, reading is affected by the set attributes(such as expire piriod time setting).

    The other set is specified by "key=em" or "emfile=<embedding file>" argument. If "<embedding file>"
    is specified for this argument, the contents as embedding data of that file are used.
    If the argument is set to "key=em", Preloaded embedding data is used. If both are omitted, the Preloaded
    embedding data will also be used.

    When the "simple" parameter is specified, the cosine similarity calculation is simplified
    under the assumption that the target embedding data is normalized.

[Command : help]: Execution time - 000ms 000us 000ns(000000000ns)

